    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Telesina',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Telesina (Teresina) is the Italian 5-card Stud. Variable deck (e.g. 5 players: 6â€“A, 36 cards). Ante; one face-down, one face-up each; highest face-up starts betting. Deal up to four face-up, one down; betting after each round. Flush ranks above full house. Variants: Con Vela (community card), with Joker (pokerissimo).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Italian poker variant (also known as Teresina). The Italian form of five-card stud, played with a stripped deck whose size depends on the number of players.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Optional',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nScore sheet (optional)\nTable space',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Ante first. Each player receives two cards (one down, one up), dealt clockwise. After first betting round, one face-up card per active player, then betting; repeat until each has four face-up and one face-down (five cards total). Dealing pattern: clockwise.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Telesina Con Vela: One card (la vela) is dealt face down to the table at the start. After the five-card hands and final betting round, la vela is turned face up and there is a final round of betting. In showdown, la vela is a community card; each player makes the best five-card hand from five in hand plus la vela.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Telesina with Joker (Con Matte): Dealer selects a rank (e.g. nines) and all cards of that rank are wild. Wild can represent any card; four of a kind plus a wild makes pokerissimo, ranking above straight flush.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Telesina con carte coperte: All cards dealt face down. After two cards each, each player reveals one card of choice before first betting round; after each subsequent deal, players choose which card to reveal so that each has one face-down and the rest face-up.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Telesina con una carta coperta: All cards dealt face up except the first and the last. Before the final betting round, each player chooses to show either the first or the last card.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
