        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest hand at showdown.',
          gameplay: '1. Ante: Each player pays an agreed ante to the pot. 2. Initial deal: Each player receives two cards (one face down, one face up), dealt clockwise. 3. First betting round: Player with highest face-up card starts; ties broken by suit (hearts highest, then diamonds, clubs, spades). 4. Further deal and betting: Another face-up card is dealt to each active player, then a betting round (opener: best pair showing, or highest card, then second card; suits break ties). This repeats until each player has four face-up and one face-down card. 5. Showdown: After the final betting round, active players reveal hands; highest hand wins the pot.',
          keyRules: [
            'Variable stripped deck: lowest rank = 11 minus number of players (e.g. 5 players use 6 to Ace, 36 cards).',
            'Hand ranking: flush ranks above full house (Italian order). Straight flush, four of a kind, flush, full house, straight, three of a kind, two pair, pair, high card.',
